    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipNumber` is a derived, read-only field computed from the owner's own fields (`customerCode` + `registrationDate`), so I implemented it the same way the existing derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`) are handled \u2014 no new stored column, no seed dependency.\n\n**Two changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `membershipNumber` read-only property to the `Owner` schema (next to `customerCode`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipNumber\", expression = \"java(membershipNumber(owner))\")` and a small single-responsibility `membershipNumber(Owner)` default method, mirroring the existing `initials(Owner)` helper:\n   ```java\n   default String membershipNumber(Owner owner) {\n       String yy = String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);\n       return owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + yy;\n   }\n   ```\n\nThis keeps DTO-derivation logic co-located with the other computed DTO fields in the mapper (its rightful place), reuses the already-stored `customerCode`/`registrationDate` rather than recomputing them, and produces the specified `<customerCode>-M<YY>` format (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`). `%02d` correctly zero-pads years like 2005 \u2192 `M05`.",
